From: Zork130 <12914881+Zork130@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6core/q6afe: custom topologies and raw module
 parameter access

Vendor speaker protection (NXP TFADSP on the OnePlus 8 Pro) runs as a module
in a custom AFE topology on the ADSP. Add what is needed to bring it up:

- q6core_register_topologies(): register custom topologies (as stored in
  the ACDB) in-band with AVCS_CMD_REGISTER_TOPOLOGIES.
- q6afe_port_set_topology(): topology sent before the port config on start.
- q6afe_port_{set,get}_module_param(): parameter access for any module.
- debugfs q6afe/cmd for poking all of the above from userspace.

